window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b353-3202644340049027.json"]={sha256:"3202644340049027f10aa9f6caa4e355b5824e3bfe457a9df674f6ab5822e76b",value:{"id":"b353","title":"道岔融雪加熱系統","titleEn":"Turnout snow-melting heaters","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"道岔融雪加熱系統以「道岔加熱熱損融冰與控制遲滯」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。道岔加熱需把熱量送到真正阻礙動作的位置，環境風、冰水相變與機械遮蔽會改變效果；耗電增加不能直接證明融雪能力改善。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops turnout heating heat loss ice melting and control hysteresis through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Turnout heating must deliver heat to locations that actually obstruct movement; wind, ice-water phase change and mechanical shielding alter effectiveness, so more electricity does not by itself prove better snow melting. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["降雪熱負載","Snow thermal load"],["加熱元件","Heating element"],["傳熱接觸","Thermal contact"],["溫度回授","Temperature feedback"],["結冰監測","Ice monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["降雪熱負載","加熱元件","傳熱接觸","溫度回授","結冰監測"],"labelsEn":["Snow thermal load","Heating element","Thermal contact","Temperature feedback","Ice monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=58.08 W。模型邊界：隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=73.48 kJ。模型邊界：冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=58.08 W. Boundary: Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=73.48 kJ. Boundary: Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b353-v16-s1","title":"加熱電功率與冰融化潛熱","titleEn":"Heater electrical power & Ice melting latent heat","description":"本階段聚焦「加熱電功率」與「冰融化潛熱」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Heater electrical power\" and \"Ice melting latent heat\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b353-v16-01","title":"加熱電功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Heater electrical power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「加熱電功率」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Heater electrical power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固定電壓下電阻升高會降低純電阻加熱功率。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 58.08 W。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗。使用隔離低壓電壓電流量測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「加熱電功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At fixed voltage, increased resistance lowers resistive heating power. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 58.08 W. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded. Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Heater electrical power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「加熱電功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Heater electrical power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-01-k1","title":"加熱電功率","titleEn":"Heater electrical power","text":"固定電壓下電阻升高會降低純電阻加熱功率。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 58.08 W。","textEn":"At fixed voltage, increased resistance lowers resistive heating power. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加熱電功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Heater electrical power\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置","固定電壓下電阻升高會降低純電阻加熱功率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations.","At fixed voltage, increased resistance lowers resistive heating power.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定電壓下電阻升高會降低純電阻加熱功率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At fixed voltage, increased resistance lowers resistive heating power. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b353-v16-02","title":"加熱電功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Heater electrical power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「加熱電功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Heater electrical power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=58.08 W。模型邊界：隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=58.08 W. Boundary: Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以隔離低壓電壓電流量測區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型加熱器端電壓、電流及接頭溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=58.08 W。模型邊界：隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=58.08 W. Boundary: Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「加熱電功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Heater electrical power\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=24 V, R=12 ohm；y=V**2/R=48 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=24 V, R=12 ohm; y=V**2/R=48 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b353-v16-03","title":"加熱電功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Heater electrical power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「加熱電功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Heater electrical power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以隔離低壓電壓電流量測區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型加熱器端電壓、電流及接頭溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「加熱電功率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model heater-terminal voltage, current and connection temperature, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Heater electrical power. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「加熱電功率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置造成偏離的合成觀察，以隔離低壓電壓電流量測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Heater electrical power, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. Explain which evidence in isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以隔離低壓電壓電流量測區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型加熱器端電壓、電流及接頭溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「加熱電功率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model heater-terminal voltage, current and connection temperature, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Heater electrical power. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「加熱電功率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出隔離低壓直流及固定電阻；不計接線端額外損耗如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置造成偏離的合成觀察，以隔離低壓電壓電流量測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Heater electrical power, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Isolated low-voltage DC and constant resistance; additional terminal losses are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. Explain which evidence in isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「加熱電功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Heater electrical power\"?","options":["本單元以隔離低壓電壓電流量測區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型加熱器端電壓、電流及接頭溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準"],"optionsEn":["Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以隔離低壓電壓電流量測區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型加熱器端電壓、電流及接頭溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b353-v16-04","title":"加熱電功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Heater electrical power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「加熱電功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Heater electrical power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置。這個失效與「加熱電功率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查隔離低壓電壓電流量測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. This failure and a measurement bias in Heater electrical power can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用隔離低壓電壓電流量測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置。這個失效與「加熱電功率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查隔離低壓電壓電流量測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. This failure and a measurement bias in Heater electrical power can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check isolated low-voltage current and voltage readings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「加熱電功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Heater electrical power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b353-v16-05","title":"冰融化潛熱：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ice melting latent heat: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「冰融化潛熱」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ice melting latent heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"融冰必須供應潛熱，即使溫度停留在相變附近。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 73.48 kJ。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫。使用冰質量與融水量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「冰融化潛熱」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Melting requires latent heat even when temperature remains near the phase change. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 73.48 kJ. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded. Use ice mass and meltwater mass as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ice melting latent heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「冰融化潛熱」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ice melting latent heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-05-k1","title":"冰融化潛熱","titleEn":"Ice melting latent heat","text":"融冰必須供應潛熱，即使溫度停留在相變附近。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 73.48 kJ。","textEn":"Melting requires latent heat even when temperature remains near the phase change. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「冰融化潛熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ice melting latent heat\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間","融冰必須供應潛熱，即使溫度停留在相變附近。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","Melting requires latent heat even when temperature remains near the phase change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"融冰必須供應潛熱，即使溫度停留在相變附近。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Melting requires latent heat even when temperature remains near the phase change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b353-v16-06","title":"冰融化潛熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Ice melting latent heat: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「冰融化潛熱」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ice melting latent heat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=73.48 kJ。模型邊界：冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=73.48 kJ. Boundary: Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以冰質量與融水量區分模型與觀察，先用教學冰樣質量、溫度平台及融水質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use ice mass and meltwater mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=73.48 kJ。模型邊界：冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=73.48 kJ. Boundary: Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「冰融化潛熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ice melting latent heat\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=66.8 kJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=0.2 kg, latent=334 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=66.8 kJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b353-v16-07","title":"冰融化潛熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ice melting latent heat: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「冰融化潛熱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ice melting latent heat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以冰質量與融水量區分模型與觀察，先用教學冰樣質量、溫度平台及融水質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「冰融化潛熱」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use ice mass and meltwater mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using teaching ice-sample mass, temperature plateau and meltwater mass, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ice melting latent heat. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「冰融化潛熱」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量造成偏離的合成觀察，以冰質量與融水量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ice melting latent heat, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. Explain which evidence in ice mass and meltwater mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以冰質量與融水量區分模型與觀察，先用教學冰樣質量、溫度平台及融水質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「冰融化潛熱」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use ice mass and meltwater mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using teaching ice-sample mass, temperature plateau and meltwater mass, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ice melting latent heat. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「冰融化潛熱」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出冰已在相變溫度且全部融化；不含預熱及融水升溫如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量造成偏離的合成觀察，以冰質量與融水量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ice melting latent heat, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Ice starts at the phase-change temperature and melts fully; preheating and warming meltwater are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. Explain which evidence in ice mass and meltwater mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「冰融化潛熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ice melting latent heat\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以冰質量與融水量區分模型與觀察，先用教學冰樣質量、溫度平台及融水質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use ice mass and meltwater mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以冰質量與融水量區分模型與觀察，先用教學冰樣質量、溫度平台及融水質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use ice mass and meltwater mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b353-v16-08","title":"冰融化潛熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ice melting latent heat: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「冰融化潛熱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ice melting latent heat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量。這個失效與「冰融化潛熱」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查冰質量與融水量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Ice melting latent heat can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check ice mass and meltwater mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用冰質量與融水量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量。這個失效與「冰融化潛熱」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查冰質量與融水量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Ice melting latent heat can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check ice mass and meltwater mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「冰融化潛熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ice melting latent heat\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間","只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b353-v16-s2","title":"理想融冰時間與對流熱損量","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration & Convective heat loss","description":"本階段聚焦「理想融冰時間」與「對流熱損量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ideal melting duration\" and \"Convective heat loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b353-v16-09","title":"理想融冰時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「理想融冰時間」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ideal melting duration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"能量除有效功率是理想時間，下限取決於損失是否忽略。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1837 s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。有效功率恆定且能量全部用於所列融化負荷。使用有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「理想融冰時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Energy divided by useful power gives an ideal time, with ignored losses making it a lower estimate. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1837 s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Useful power is constant and all its energy serves the declared melting load. Use useful heat input and melting completion time as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ideal melting duration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W；y=E*1000/P=1670 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W; y=E*1000/P=1670 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「理想融冰時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ideal melting duration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-09-k1","title":"理想融冰時間","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration","text":"能量除有效功率是理想時間，下限取決於損失是否忽略。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1837 s。","textEn":"Energy divided by useful power gives an ideal time, with ignored losses making it a lower estimate. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「理想融冰時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ideal melting duration\" is correct?","options":["能量除有效功率是理想時間，下限取決於損失是否忽略。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足"],"optionsEn":["Energy divided by useful power gives an ideal time, with ignored losses making it a lower estimate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"能量除有效功率是理想時間，下限取決於損失是否忽略。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Energy divided by useful power gives an ideal time, with ignored losses making it a lower estimate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b353-v16-10","title":"理想融冰時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「理想融冰時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ideal melting duration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W；y=E*1000/P=1670 s。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=1837 s。模型邊界：有效功率恆定且能量全部用於所列融化負荷；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W; y=E*1000/P=1670 s. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=1837 s. Boundary: Useful power is constant and all its energy serves the declared melting load; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型有效熱功率、剩餘冰量及完成時間建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use useful heat input and melting completion time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W；y=E*1000/P=1670 s。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=1837 s。模型邊界：有效功率恆定且能量全部用於所列融化負荷；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W; y=E*1000/P=1670 s. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=1837 s. Boundary: Useful power is constant and all its energy serves the declared melting load; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「理想融冰時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ideal melting duration\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W；y=E*1000/P=1670 s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W; y=E*1000/P=1670 s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W；y=E*1000/P=1670 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=66.8 kJ, P=40 W; y=E*1000/P=1670 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b353-v16-11","title":"理想融冰時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「理想融冰時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ideal melting duration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型有效熱功率、剩餘冰量及完成時間建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「理想融冰時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use useful heat input and melting completion time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model useful thermal power, remaining ice and completion time, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ideal melting duration. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「理想融冰時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效功率恆定且能量全部用於所列融化負荷如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ideal melting duration, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Useful power is constant and all its energy serves the declared melting load. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. Explain which evidence in useful heat input and melting completion time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型有效熱功率、剩餘冰量及完成時間建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「理想融冰時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use useful heat input and melting completion time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model useful thermal power, remaining ice and completion time, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ideal melting duration. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「理想融冰時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效功率恆定且能量全部用於所列融化負荷如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ideal melting duration, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Useful power is constant and all its energy serves the declared melting load. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. Explain which evidence in useful heat input and melting completion time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「理想融冰時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ideal melting duration\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差","本單元以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型有效熱功率、剩餘冰量及完成時間建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.","Use useful heat input and melting completion time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型有效熱功率、剩餘冰量及完成時間建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use useful heat input and melting completion time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b353-v16-12","title":"理想融冰時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ideal melting duration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「理想融冰時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ideal melting duration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間。這個失效與「理想融冰時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. This failure and a measurement bias in Ideal melting duration can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check useful heat input and melting completion time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間。這個失效與「理想融冰時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查有效熱輸入與融冰完成時刻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. This failure and a measurement bias in Ideal melting duration can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check useful heat input and melting completion time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理想融冰時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ideal melting duration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足"],"optionsEn":["Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b353-v16-13","title":"對流熱損量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Convective heat loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「對流熱損量」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Convective heat loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"對流熱損取決於暴露面積與環境條件。本模型把 h 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66 W。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。暴露面積、換熱係數及溫差固定；不含輻射和導熱。使用表面氣溫與風況作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；風速增加會使原有效功率不足，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對流熱損量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Convection loss depends on exposed area and environmental conditions. In this model, h is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 66 W. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Exposed area, heat-transfer coefficient and temperature difference are constant; radiation and conduction are excluded. Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Convective heat loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K；y=h*A*dT=60 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K; y=h*A*dT=60 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「對流熱損量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Convective heat loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-13-k1","title":"對流熱損量","titleEn":"Convective heat loss","text":"對流熱損取決於暴露面積與環境條件。本模型把 h 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66 W。","textEn":"Convection loss depends on exposed area and environmental conditions. In this model, h is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「對流熱損量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Convective heat loss\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足","對流熱損取決於暴露面積與環境條件。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient.","Convection loss depends on exposed area and environmental conditions.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對流熱損取決於暴露面積與環境條件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Convection loss depends on exposed area and environmental conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b353-v16-14","title":"對流熱損量：定量估算","titleEn":"Convective heat loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對流熱損量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Convective heat loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K；y=h*A*dT=60 W。只把 h 增加百分之十，y=66 W。模型邊界：暴露面積、換熱係數及溫差固定；不含輻射和導熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K; y=h*A*dT=60 W. Increasing only h with a ten-percent increase gives y=66 W. Boundary: Exposed area, heat-transfer coefficient and temperature difference are constant; radiation and conduction are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以表面氣溫與風況區分模型與觀察，先用模型表面與空氣溫度、風速及暴露面積建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K；y=h*A*dT=60 W。只把 h 增加百分之十，y=66 W。模型邊界：暴露面積、換熱係數及溫差固定；不含輻射和導熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K; y=h*A*dT=60 W. Increasing only h with a ten-percent increase gives y=66 W. Boundary: Exposed area, heat-transfer coefficient and temperature difference are constant; radiation and conduction are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「對流熱損量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Convective heat loss\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K；y=h*A*dT=60 W。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K; y=h*A*dT=60 W."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K；y=h*A*dT=60 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=15 W/m2K, A=0.2 m2, dT=20 K; y=h*A*dT=60 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b353-v16-15","title":"對流熱損量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Convective heat loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對流熱損量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Convective heat loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以表面氣溫與風況區分模型與觀察，先用模型表面與空氣溫度、風速及暴露面積建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「對流熱損量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model surface and air temperature, air speed and exposed area, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Convective heat loss. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「對流熱損量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出暴露面積、換熱係數及溫差固定；不含輻射和導熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由風速增加會使原有效功率不足造成偏離的合成觀察，以表面氣溫與風況說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Convective heat loss, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Exposed area, heat-transfer coefficient and temperature difference are constant; radiation and conduction are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. Explain which evidence in surface-air temperature and wind conditions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：風速增加會使原有效功率不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以表面氣溫與風況區分模型與觀察，先用模型表面與空氣溫度、風速及暴露面積建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「對流熱損量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model surface and air temperature, air speed and exposed area, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Convective heat loss. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「對流熱損量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出暴露面積、換熱係數及溫差固定；不含輻射和導熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由風速增加會使原有效功率不足造成偏離的合成觀察，以表面氣溫與風況說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Convective heat loss, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Exposed area, heat-transfer coefficient and temperature difference are constant; radiation and conduction are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. Explain which evidence in surface-air temperature and wind conditions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「對流熱損量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Convective heat loss\"?","options":["本單元以表面氣溫與風況區分模型與觀察，先用模型表面與空氣溫度、風速及暴露面積建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置"],"optionsEn":["Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以表面氣溫與風況區分模型與觀察，先用模型表面與空氣溫度、風速及暴露面積建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use surface-air temperature and wind conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b353-v16-16","title":"對流熱損量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Convective heat loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對流熱損量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Convective heat loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"風速增加會使原有效功率不足。這個失效與「對流熱損量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查表面氣溫與風況，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. This failure and a measurement bias in Convective heat loss can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check surface-air temperature and wind conditions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用表面氣溫與風況作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；風速增加會使原有效功率不足，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"風速增加會使原有效功率不足。這個失效與「對流熱損量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查表面氣溫與風況，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. This failure and a measurement bias in Convective heat loss can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check surface-air temperature and wind conditions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對流熱損量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Convective heat loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","風速增加會使原有效功率不足。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"風速增加會使原有效功率不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b353-v16-s3","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷與加熱效率比例","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand & Useful heating fraction","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼件顯熱負荷」與「加熱效率比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Steel sensible-heat demand\" and \"Useful heating fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b353-v16-17","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「鋼件顯熱負荷」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel sensible-heat demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"先加熱鋼件所需熱量與融冰潛熱分屬不同帳。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 kJ。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。鋼件溫升均勻且比熱固定；不計冰的顯熱或潛熱。使用鋼件質量與平均溫升作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼件顯熱負荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Heating steel and melting ice are separate energy accounts. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 16.5 kJ. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Steel temperature rise is uniform and heat capacity constant; ice sensible or latent heat is excluded. Use steel mass and mean temperature rise as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Large heat capacity creates start-up delay; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Steel sensible-heat demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼件顯熱負荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Steel sensible-heat demand”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-17-k1","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand","text":"先加熱鋼件所需熱量與融冰潛熱分屬不同帳。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 kJ。","textEn":"Heating steel and melting ice are separate energy accounts. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼件顯熱負荷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Steel sensible-heat demand\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","先加熱鋼件所需熱量與融冰潛熱分屬不同帳。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","Heating steel and melting ice are separate energy accounts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先加熱鋼件所需熱量與融冰潛熱分屬不同帳。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Heating steel and melting ice are separate energy accounts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b353-v16-18","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷：定量估算","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼件顯熱負荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel sensible-heat demand” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=16.5 kJ。模型邊界：鋼件溫升均勻且比熱固定；不計冰的顯熱或潛熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 kJ. Boundary: Steel temperature rise is uniform and heat capacity constant; ice sensible or latent heat is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以鋼件質量與平均溫升區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼件秤重、多點溫度與平均溫升建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use steel mass and mean temperature rise to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=16.5 kJ。模型邊界：鋼件溫升均勻且比熱固定；不計冰的顯熱或潛熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 kJ. Boundary: Steel temperature rise is uniform and heat capacity constant; ice sensible or latent heat is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼件顯熱負荷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Steel sensible-heat demand\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=3 kg, c=500 J/kgK, dT=10 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=15 kJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b353-v16-19","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼件顯熱負荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel sensible-heat demand” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以鋼件質量與平均溫升區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼件秤重、多點溫度與平均溫升建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼件顯熱負荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use steel mass and mean temperature rise to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model steel mass, distributed temperatures and mean temperature rise, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Steel sensible-heat demand. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「鋼件顯熱負荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出鋼件溫升均勻且比熱固定；不計冰的顯熱或潛熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼件質量與平均溫升說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Steel sensible-heat demand, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steel temperature rise is uniform and heat capacity constant; ice sensible or latent heat is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. Explain which evidence in steel mass and mean temperature rise distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以鋼件質量與平均溫升區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼件秤重、多點溫度與平均溫升建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼件顯熱負荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use steel mass and mean temperature rise to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model steel mass, distributed temperatures and mean temperature rise, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Steel sensible-heat demand. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「鋼件顯熱負荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出鋼件溫升均勻且比熱固定；不計冰的顯熱或潛熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼件質量與平均溫升說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Steel sensible-heat demand, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steel temperature rise is uniform and heat capacity constant; ice sensible or latent heat is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. Explain which evidence in steel mass and mean temperature rise distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼件顯熱負荷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Steel sensible-heat demand\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以鋼件質量與平均溫升區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼件秤重、多點溫度與平均溫升建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use steel mass and mean temperature rise to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以鋼件質量與平均溫升區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼件秤重、多點溫度與平均溫升建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use steel mass and mean temperature rise to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b353-v16-20","title":"鋼件顯熱負荷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Steel sensible-heat demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼件顯熱負荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel sensible-heat demand” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲。這個失效與「鋼件顯熱負荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼件質量與平均溫升，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. This failure and a measurement bias in Steel sensible-heat demand can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check steel mass and mean temperature rise rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用鋼件質量與平均溫升作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲。這個失效與「鋼件顯熱負荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼件質量與平均溫升，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. This failure and a measurement bias in Steel sensible-heat demand can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check steel mass and mean temperature rise rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼件顯熱負荷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Steel sensible-heat demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","Large heat capacity creates start-up delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large heat capacity creates start-up delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b353-v16-21","title":"加熱效率比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Useful heating fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「加熱效率比例」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Useful heating fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有效熱量比例須定義送到哪個作用區。本模型把 useful 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 68.75 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。作用區與時間窗明確且兩功率同步；不把輸入電功率全算有效熱。使用作用區熱量與輸入電能作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「加熱效率比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Useful fraction needs a defined target region. In this model, useful is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 68.75 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Target region and interval are defined and powers synchronous; input electrical power is not all useful heat. Use target-zone heat and electrical input as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Useful heating fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：useful=30 W, input=48 W；y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: useful=30 W, input=48 W; y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「加熱效率比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Useful heating fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-21-k1","title":"加熱效率比例","titleEn":"Useful heating fraction","text":"有效熱量比例須定義送到哪個作用區。本模型把 useful 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 68.75 percent。","textEn":"Useful fraction needs a defined target region. In this model, useful is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加熱效率比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Useful heating fraction\" is correct?","options":["有效熱量比例須定義送到哪個作用區。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動"],"optionsEn":["Useful fraction needs a defined target region.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有效熱量比例須定義送到哪個作用區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Useful fraction needs a defined target region. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b353-v16-22","title":"加熱效率比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Useful heating fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「加熱效率比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Useful heating fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：useful=30 W, input=48 W；y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent。只把 useful 增加百分之十，y=68.75 percent。模型邊界：作用區與時間窗明確且兩功率同步；不把輸入電功率全算有效熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: useful=30 W, input=48 W; y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent. Increasing only useful with a ten-percent increase gives y=68.75 percent. Boundary: Target region and interval are defined and powers synchronous; input electrical power is not all useful heat; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以作用區熱量與輸入電能區分模型與觀察，先用作用區熱量帳、輸入電功率及其他散熱路徑建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use target-zone heat and electrical input to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：useful=30 W, input=48 W；y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent。只把 useful 增加百分之十，y=68.75 percent。模型邊界：作用區與時間窗明確且兩功率同步；不把輸入電功率全算有效熱；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: useful=30 W, input=48 W; y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent. Increasing only useful with a ten-percent increase gives y=68.75 percent. Boundary: Target region and interval are defined and powers synchronous; input electrical power is not all useful heat; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「加熱效率比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Useful heating fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：useful=30 W, input=48 W；y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: useful=30 W, input=48 W; y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：useful=30 W, input=48 W；y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: useful=30 W, input=48 W; y=useful/input*100=62.5 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b353-v16-23","title":"加熱效率比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Useful heating fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「加熱效率比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Useful heating fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以作用區熱量與輸入電能區分模型與觀察，先用作用區熱量帳、輸入電功率及其他散熱路徑建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「加熱效率比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use target-zone heat and electrical input to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using target-zone heat account, electrical input power and other heat-loss paths, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Useful heating fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「加熱效率比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出作用區與時間窗明確且兩功率同步；不把輸入電功率全算有效熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰造成偏離的合成觀察，以作用區熱量與輸入電能說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Useful heating fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Target region and interval are defined and powers synchronous; input electrical power is not all useful heat. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. Explain which evidence in target-zone heat and electrical input distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以作用區熱量與輸入電能區分模型與觀察，先用作用區熱量帳、輸入電功率及其他散熱路徑建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「加熱效率比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use target-zone heat and electrical input to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using target-zone heat account, electrical input power and other heat-loss paths, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Useful heating fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「加熱效率比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出作用區與時間窗明確且兩功率同步；不把輸入電功率全算有效熱如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰造成偏離的合成觀察，以作用區熱量與輸入電能說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Useful heating fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Target region and interval are defined and powers synchronous; input electrical power is not all useful heat. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. Explain which evidence in target-zone heat and electrical input distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「加熱效率比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Useful heating fraction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間","本單元以作用區熱量與輸入電能區分模型與觀察，先用作用區熱量帳、輸入電功率及其他散熱路徑建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","Use target-zone heat and electrical input to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以作用區熱量與輸入電能區分模型與觀察，先用作用區熱量帳、輸入電功率及其他散熱路徑建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use target-zone heat and electrical input to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b353-v16-24","title":"加熱效率比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Useful heating fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「加熱效率比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Useful heating fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰。這個失效與「加熱效率比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查作用區熱量與輸入電能，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. This failure and a measurement bias in Useful heating fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check target-zone heat and electrical input rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用作用區熱量與輸入電能作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰。這個失效與「加熱效率比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查作用區熱量與輸入電能，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. This failure and a measurement bias in Useful heating fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check target-zone heat and electrical input rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「加熱效率比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Useful heating fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動"],"optionsEn":["Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b353-v16-s4","title":"控制遲滯帶寬與溫度時間常數","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width & Thermal time constant","description":"本階段聚焦「控制遲滯帶寬」與「溫度時間常數」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control hysteresis width\" and \"Thermal time constant\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b353-v16-25","title":"控制遲滯帶寬：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「控制遲滯帶寬」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Control hysteresis width” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"開關門檻差可以降低頻繁切換，但也改變溫度波動。本模型把 off 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加攝氏一度，輸出增加為 4 K。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。開啟與關閉溫度在同一尺度；只算門檻差，不預測動態超調。使用開關事件與溫度時間序列作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「控制遲滯帶寬」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Threshold separation reduces rapid switching but changes temperature fluctuation. In this model, off is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. An increase of one degree celsius means the output increases to 4 K. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. On and off temperatures use one scale; only threshold separation is calculated, not dynamic overshoot. Use switching events and temperature trace as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Control hysteresis width” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：off=5 degC, on=2 degC；y=off-on=3 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: off=5 degC, on=2 degC; y=off-on=3 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「控制遲滯帶寬」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Control hysteresis width”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-25-k1","title":"控制遲滯帶寬","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width","text":"開關門檻差可以降低頻繁切換，但也改變溫度波動。本模型把 off 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加攝氏一度，輸出增加為 4 K。","textEn":"Threshold separation reduces rapid switching but changes temperature fluctuation. In this model, off is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制遲滯帶寬」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control hysteresis width\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動","開關門檻差可以降低頻繁切換，但也改變溫度波動。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter.","Threshold separation reduces rapid switching but changes temperature fluctuation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開關門檻差可以降低頻繁切換，但也改變溫度波動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Threshold separation reduces rapid switching but changes temperature fluctuation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b353-v16-26","title":"控制遲滯帶寬：定量估算","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「控制遲滯帶寬」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Control hysteresis width” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：off=5 degC, on=2 degC；y=off-on=3 K。只把 off 增加攝氏一度，y=4 K。模型邊界：開啟與關閉溫度在同一尺度；只算門檻差，不預測動態超調；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: off=5 degC, on=2 degC; y=off-on=3 K. Increasing only off with an increase of one degree Celsius gives y=4 K. Boundary: On and off temperatures use one scale; only threshold separation is calculated, not dynamic overshoot; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以開關事件與溫度時間序列區分模型與觀察，先用合成溫度訊號、開關事件及注入雜訊建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use switching events and temperature trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：off=5 degC, on=2 degC；y=off-on=3 K。只把 off 增加攝氏一度，y=4 K。模型邊界：開啟與關閉溫度在同一尺度；只算門檻差，不預測動態超調；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: off=5 degC, on=2 degC; y=off-on=3 K. Increasing only off with an increase of one degree Celsius gives y=4 K. Boundary: On and off temperatures use one scale; only threshold separation is calculated, not dynamic overshoot; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制遲滯帶寬」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control hysteresis width\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：off=5 degC, on=2 degC；y=off-on=3 K。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: off=5 degC, on=2 degC; y=off-on=3 K."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：off=5 degC, on=2 degC；y=off-on=3 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: off=5 degC, on=2 degC; y=off-on=3 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b353-v16-27","title":"控制遲滯帶寬：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「控制遲滯帶寬」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Control hysteresis width” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以開關事件與溫度時間序列區分模型與觀察，先用合成溫度訊號、開關事件及注入雜訊建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「控制遲滯帶寬」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use switching events and temperature trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic temperature signal, switching events and injected noise, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Control hysteresis width. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「控制遲滯帶寬」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出開啟與關閉溫度在同一尺度；只算門檻差，不預測動態超調如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動造成偏離的合成觀察，以開關事件與溫度時間序列說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Control hysteresis width, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: On and off temperatures use one scale; only threshold separation is calculated, not dynamic overshoot. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. Explain which evidence in switching events and temperature trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以開關事件與溫度時間序列區分模型與觀察，先用合成溫度訊號、開關事件及注入雜訊建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「控制遲滯帶寬」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use switching events and temperature trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic temperature signal, switching events and injected noise, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Control hysteresis width. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「控制遲滯帶寬」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出開啟與關閉溫度在同一尺度；只算門檻差，不預測動態超調如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動造成偏離的合成觀察，以開關事件與溫度時間序列說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Control hysteresis width, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: On and off temperatures use one scale; only threshold separation is calculated, not dynamic overshoot. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. Explain which evidence in switching events and temperature trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制遲滯帶寬」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control hysteresis width\"?","options":["本單元以開關事件與溫度時間序列區分模型與觀察，先用合成溫度訊號、開關事件及注入雜訊建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足"],"optionsEn":["Use switching events and temperature trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以開關事件與溫度時間序列區分模型與觀察，先用合成溫度訊號、開關事件及注入雜訊建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use switching events and temperature trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b353-v16-28","title":"控制遲滯帶寬：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control hysteresis width: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「控制遲滯帶寬」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Control hysteresis width” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動。這個失效與「控制遲滯帶寬」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查開關事件與溫度時間序列，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. This failure and a measurement bias in Control hysteresis width can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check switching events and temperature trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用開關事件與溫度時間序列作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動。這個失效與「控制遲滯帶寬」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查開關事件與溫度時間序列，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. This failure and a measurement bias in Control hysteresis width can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check switching events and temperature trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制遲滯帶寬」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control hysteresis width\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b353-v16-29","title":"溫度時間常數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal time constant: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「溫度時間常數」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal time constant” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"集中模型的時間常數為熱容量除總散熱導納。本模型把 C 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 330 s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均溫單熱容節點及線性散熱導納；不含相變。使用階躍加熱的溫度反應作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溫度時間常數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A lumped thermal time constant is heat capacity divided by heat-loss conductance. In this model, C is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 330 s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. One uniform-temperature capacitance node and linear heat-loss conductance; phase change is excluded. Use temperature response to a heating step as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Steady temperature does not determine heating speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal time constant” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K；y=C/H=300 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K; y=C/H=300 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「溫度時間常數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal time constant”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-29-k1","title":"溫度時間常數","titleEn":"Thermal time constant","text":"集中模型的時間常數為熱容量除總散熱導納。本模型把 C 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 330 s。","textEn":"A lumped thermal time constant is heat capacity divided by heat-loss conductance. In this model, C is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度時間常數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal time constant\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪","集中模型的時間常數為熱容量除總散熱導納。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","A lumped thermal time constant is heat capacity divided by heat-loss conductance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"集中模型的時間常數為熱容量除總散熱導納。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A lumped thermal time constant is heat capacity divided by heat-loss conductance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b353-v16-30","title":"溫度時間常數：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal time constant: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「溫度時間常數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal time constant” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K；y=C/H=300 s。只把 C 增加百分之十，y=330 s。模型邊界：均溫單熱容節點及線性散熱導納；不含相變；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K; y=C/H=300 s. Increasing only C with a ten-percent increase gives y=330 s. Boundary: One uniform-temperature capacitance node and linear heat-loss conductance; phase change is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以階躍加熱的溫度反應區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型階躍功率、環境溫度及完整升溫曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use temperature response to a heating step to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K；y=C/H=300 s。只把 C 增加百分之十，y=330 s。模型邊界：均溫單熱容節點及線性散熱導納；不含相變；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K; y=C/H=300 s. Increasing only C with a ten-percent increase gives y=330 s. Boundary: One uniform-temperature capacitance node and linear heat-loss conductance; phase change is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度時間常數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal time constant\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K；y=C/H=300 s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K; y=C/H=300 s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K；y=C/H=300 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: C=1500 J/K, H=5 W/K; y=C/H=300 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b353-v16-31","title":"溫度時間常數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal time constant: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「溫度時間常數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal time constant” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以階躍加熱的溫度反應區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型階躍功率、環境溫度及完整升溫曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫度時間常數」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use temperature response to a heating step to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model power step, ambient temperature and full heating trace, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal time constant. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「溫度時間常數」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫單熱容節點及線性散熱導納；不含相變如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準造成偏離的合成觀察，以階躍加熱的溫度反應說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal time constant, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One uniform-temperature capacitance node and linear heat-loss conductance; phase change is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. Explain which evidence in temperature response to a heating step distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以階躍加熱的溫度反應區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型階躍功率、環境溫度及完整升溫曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫度時間常數」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use temperature response to a heating step to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model power step, ambient temperature and full heating trace, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal time constant. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「溫度時間常數」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫單熱容節點及線性散熱導納；不含相變如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準造成偏離的合成觀察，以階躍加熱的溫度反應說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal time constant, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One uniform-temperature capacitance node and linear heat-loss conductance; phase change is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. Explain which evidence in temperature response to a heating step distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度時間常數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal time constant\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以階躍加熱的溫度反應區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型階躍功率、環境溫度及完整升溫曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use temperature response to a heating step to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以階躍加熱的溫度反應區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型階躍功率、環境溫度及完整升溫曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use temperature response to a heating step to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b353-v16-32","title":"溫度時間常數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal time constant: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「溫度時間常數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal time constant” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準。這個失效與「溫度時間常數」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查階躍加熱的溫度反應，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal time constant can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature response to a heating step rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用階躍加熱的溫度反應作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Steady temperature does not determine heating speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準。這個失效與「溫度時間常數」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查階躍加熱的溫度反應，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal time constant can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature response to a heating step rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度時間常數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal time constant\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪","用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","Steady temperature does not determine heating speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用穩態溫度推論升溫速度會失準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Steady temperature does not determine heating speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b353-v16-s5","title":"降雪水當量負荷與感測器偏差餘量","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load & Sensor-bias reserve","description":"本階段聚焦「降雪水當量負荷」與「感測器偏差餘量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Snow water-equivalent load\" and \"Sensor-bias reserve\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b353-v16-33","title":"降雪水當量負荷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「降雪水當量負荷」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Snow water-equivalent load” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪密度改變會讓同厚度有不同融化負荷。本模型把 area 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.1 kg。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。雪深與雪密度在面積內均勻；結果是質量而非水當量厚度。使用雪深面積與密度樣本作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「降雪水當量負荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Snow density changes melting load even at equal depth. In this model, area is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.1 kg. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Snow depth and density are uniform over area; the result is mass rather than water-equivalent depth. Use snow depth, area and density samples as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Snow water-equivalent load” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3；y=area*depth*rho=1 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3; y=area*depth*rho=1 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「降雪水當量負荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Snow water-equivalent load”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-33-k1","title":"降雪水當量負荷","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load","text":"雪密度改變會讓同厚度有不同融化負荷。本模型把 area 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.1 kg。","textEn":"Snow density changes melting load even at equal depth. In this model, area is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「降雪水當量負荷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Snow water-equivalent load\" is correct?","options":["雪密度改變會讓同厚度有不同融化負荷。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差"],"optionsEn":["Snow density changes melting load even at equal depth.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雪密度改變會讓同厚度有不同融化負荷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Snow density changes melting load even at equal depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b353-v16-34","title":"降雪水當量負荷：定量估算","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「降雪水當量負荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Snow water-equivalent load” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3；y=area*depth*rho=1 kg。只把 area 增加百分之十，y=1.1 kg。模型邊界：雪深與雪密度在面積內均勻；結果是質量而非水當量厚度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3; y=area*depth*rho=1 kg. Increasing only area with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.1 kg. Boundary: Snow depth and density are uniform over area; the result is mass rather than water-equivalent depth; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以雪深面積與密度樣本區分模型與觀察，先用模型覆雪面積、深度網格及定容雪樣質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use snow depth, area and density samples to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3；y=area*depth*rho=1 kg。只把 area 增加百分之十，y=1.1 kg。模型邊界：雪深與雪密度在面積內均勻；結果是質量而非水當量厚度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3; y=area*depth*rho=1 kg. Increasing only area with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.1 kg. Boundary: Snow depth and density are uniform over area; the result is mass rather than water-equivalent depth; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「降雪水當量負荷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Snow water-equivalent load\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只計溫升會低估融冰所需熱量","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3；y=area*depth*rho=1 kg。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風速增加會使原有效功率不足"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Counting only temperature rise understates melting energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3; y=area*depth*rho=1 kg.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Increased wind can make previously adequate power insufficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3；y=area*depth*rho=1 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: area=0.5 m2, depth=0.02 m, rho=100 kg/m3; y=area*depth*rho=1 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b353-v16-35","title":"降雪水當量負荷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「降雪水當量負荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Snow water-equivalent load” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以雪深面積與密度樣本區分模型與觀察，先用模型覆雪面積、深度網格及定容雪樣質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「降雪水當量負荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use snow depth, area and density samples to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model snow-covered area, depth grid and fixed-volume snow-sample mass, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Snow water-equivalent load. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「降雪水當量負荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出雪深與雪密度在面積內均勻；結果是質量而非水當量厚度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪造成偏離的合成觀察，以雪深面積與密度樣本說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Snow water-equivalent load, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Snow depth and density are uniform over area; the result is mass rather than water-equivalent depth. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. Explain which evidence in snow depth, area and density samples distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以雪深面積與密度樣本區分模型與觀察，先用模型覆雪面積、深度網格及定容雪樣質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「降雪水當量負荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use snow depth, area and density samples to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model snow-covered area, depth grid and fixed-volume snow-sample mass, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Snow water-equivalent load. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「降雪水當量負荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出雪深與雪密度在面積內均勻；結果是質量而非水當量厚度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪造成偏離的合成觀察，以雪深面積與密度樣本說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Snow water-equivalent load, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Snow depth and density are uniform over area; the result is mass rather than water-equivalent depth. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. Explain which evidence in snow depth, area and density samples distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「降雪水當量負荷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Snow water-equivalent load\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：加熱位置錯誤會使高耗電仍無法解除卡冰","本單元以雪深面積與密度樣本區分模型與觀察，先用模型覆雪面積、深度網格及定容雪樣質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong heater placement can consume power without releasing trapped ice.","Use snow depth, area and density samples to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以雪深面積與密度樣本區分模型與觀察，先用模型覆雪面積、深度網格及定容雪樣質量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use snow depth, area and density samples to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b353-v16-36","title":"降雪水當量負荷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Snow water-equivalent load: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「降雪水當量負荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Snow water-equivalent load” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪。這個失效與「降雪水當量負荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查雪深面積與密度樣本，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. This failure and a measurement bias in Snow water-equivalent load can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check snow depth, area and density samples rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用雪深面積與密度樣本作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪。這個失效與「降雪水當量負荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查雪深面積與密度樣本，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. This failure and a measurement bias in Snow water-equivalent load can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check snow depth, area and density samples rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「降雪水當量負荷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Snow water-equivalent load\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差"],"optionsEn":["Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只按雪深判斷負荷會忽略濕雪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Depth-only estimates overlook wet-snow mass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b353-v16-37","title":"感測器偏差餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sensor-bias reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「感測器偏差餘量」如何影響道岔融雪加熱系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sensor-bias reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Turnout snow-melting heaters”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"正偏差會讓控制器以為比實際更溫暖。本模型把 target 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加攝氏一度，輸出增加為 2.8 degC。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。偏差定義為顯示減真值且為常數；溫差以開爾文相減。使用獨立參考溫度與控制讀值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「感測器偏差餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Positive bias makes the controller believe conditions are warmer than reality. In this model, target is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. An increase of one degree celsius means the output increases to 2.8 degC. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Bias is indicated minus true temperature and constant; a kelvin temperature difference is subtracted. Use independent reference temperature and control reading as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sensor-bias reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K；y=target-bias=1.8 degC。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K; y=target-bias=1.8 degC.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「感測器偏差餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sensor-bias reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-37-k1","title":"感測器偏差餘量","titleEn":"Sensor-bias reserve","text":"正偏差會讓控制器以為比實際更溫暖。本模型把 target 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加攝氏一度，輸出增加為 2.8 degC。","textEn":"Positive bias makes the controller believe conditions are warmer than reality. In this model, target is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「感測器偏差餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sensor-bias reserve\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差","正偏差會讓控制器以為比實際更溫暖。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.","Positive bias makes the controller believe conditions are warmer than reality.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正偏差會讓控制器以為比實際更溫暖。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Positive bias makes the controller believe conditions are warmer than reality. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b353-v16-38","title":"感測器偏差餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Sensor-bias reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「感測器偏差餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sensor-bias reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K；y=target-bias=1.8 degC。只把 target 增加攝氏一度，y=2.8 degC。模型邊界：偏差定義為顯示減真值且為常數；溫差以開爾文相減；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K; y=target-bias=1.8 degC. Increasing only target with an increase of one degree Celsius gives y=2.8 degC. Boundary: Bias is indicated minus true temperature and constant; a kelvin temperature difference is subtracted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型控制讀值、獨立溫度基準及貼附狀態建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use independent reference temperature and control reading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K；y=target-bias=1.8 degC。只把 target 增加攝氏一度，y=2.8 degC。模型邊界：偏差定義為顯示減真值且為常數；溫差以開爾文相減；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K; y=target-bias=1.8 degC. Increasing only target with an increase of one degree Celsius gives y=2.8 degC. Boundary: Bias is indicated minus true temperature and constant; a kelvin temperature difference is subtracted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「感測器偏差餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sensor-bias reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：風冷與排水帶熱會延長實際時間","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：巨大熱容量會造成啟動延遲","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K；y=target-bias=1.8 degC。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wind cooling and warm drainage extend real duration.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Large heat capacity creates start-up delay.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K; y=target-bias=1.8 degC."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K；y=target-bias=1.8 degC。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: target=3 degC, bias=1.2 K; y=target-bias=1.8 degC. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b353-v16-39","title":"感測器偏差餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sensor-bias reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「感測器偏差餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sensor-bias reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型控制讀值、獨立溫度基準及貼附狀態建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「感測器偏差餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use independent reference temperature and control reading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model control reading, independent temperature reference and attachment condition, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sensor-bias reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「感測器偏差餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出偏差定義為顯示減真值且為常數；溫差以開爾文相減如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sensor-bias reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Bias is indicated minus true temperature and constant; a kelvin temperature difference is subtracted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. Explain which evidence in independent reference temperature and control reading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型控制讀值、獨立溫度基準及貼附狀態建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「感測器偏差餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use independent reference temperature and control reading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage model control reading, independent temperature reference and attachment condition, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sensor-bias reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「感測器偏差餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出偏差定義為顯示減真值且為常數；溫差以開爾文相減如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sensor-bias reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Bias is indicated minus true temperature and constant; a kelvin temperature difference is subtracted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. Explain which evidence in independent reference temperature and control reading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「感測器偏差餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sensor-bias reserve\"?","options":["本單元以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型控制讀值、獨立溫度基準及貼附狀態建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：無遲滯且有雜訊時可能快速抖動"],"optionsEn":["Use independent reference temperature and control reading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Noise without hysteresis can cause rapid chatter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以獨立參考溫度與控制讀值區分模型與觀察，先用低壓模型控制讀值、獨立溫度基準及貼附狀態建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use independent reference temperature and control reading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b353-v16-40","title":"感測器偏差餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sensor-bias reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b353-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「感測器偏差餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sensor-bias reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差。這個失效與「感測器偏差餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查獨立參考溫度與控制讀值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Sensor-bias reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check independent reference temperature and control reading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用獨立參考溫度與控制讀值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b353-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差。這個失效與「感測器偏差餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查獨立參考溫度與控制讀值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Sensor-bias reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check independent reference temperature and control reading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b353-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「感測器偏差餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sensor-bias reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點電阻會把熱量耗在不需要的位置"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Contact resistance dissipates heat at unwanted locations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測器貼附不良會增加環境偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor sensor attachment increases ambient bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b353-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b353-en.svg"}};
